{
  "info": {
    "name": "Quelorax Backend API",
    "description": "Backend REST API for the Quelorax Queue Management System (Spring Boot). Import the accompanying environment too, then run 'Login (Admin)' first to auto-capture a JWT into {{token}}.\n\nQuelorax Backend API \u2014 routed through the api-gateway (http://localhost:8080), which now sits in front of 4 independent microservices: auth-service (:8081), queue-service (:8082), notification-service (:8083). Every request in this collection still targets {{base_url}} = the gateway, exactly as before \u2014 nothing here needs to change to work against the new architecture. See README-MICROSERVICES.md in the backend folder for details, and the 'Direct-to-service (advanced/debug)' folder below if you ever want to bypass the gateway and hit a service directly.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "base_url",
      "value": "http://localhost:8080"
    },
    {
      "key": "token",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "userId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "departmentId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "tokenId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "otp",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "google_id_token",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
